          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Kakeya Set
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            that contains a unit line segment for every
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direction"} direction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ball"} ball
            is a Kakeya set.
          %p
            The
            %em Kakeya Set Conjecture
            asserts that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            Kakeya set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\subset\mathbb{R}^n
            has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+dimension"} Hausdorff dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %h2#xray_transform X-Ray Transform
          %p
            The
            %em X-ray transform
            is the operator
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi l
                  %mi f
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %mi λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{X} f(l) \coloneqq \int_l f\,d\lambda(x),
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi l
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l\subset\mathbb{R}^n
            is a line, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lebesgue+measure"} Lebesgue measure
            on the line.
          %p
            Define a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_n
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi ℙ
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                  %mo ;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M_n = \big\{(\sigma, x)\in \mathbb{P}^{n-1}\times\mathbb{R}^n \mid \langle x,\sigma\rangle = 0\big\};
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℙ
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo ±
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P}^{n-1} \coloneqq S^{n-1}/\{\pm\}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+space"} projective space
            of lines in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            that pass through the origin, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\sigma,x)
            represents a line that passes through
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            with direction
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          %p
            We endow
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_n
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure"} measure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            invariant under rigid motions.
          %p
            It is an open problem to determine the exponents
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi p
                  %mo ,
                  %mi q
                  %mo ,
                  %mi r
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\le p,q,r\le\infty
            for which the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inequality"} inequality
            holds:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo ‖
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                      %mi f
                      %mo ‖
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi L
                        %mi q
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %mi σ
                      %mo ↦
                      %msubsup
                        %mi L
                        %mi x
                        %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≤
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo ‖
                      %mi f
                      %mo ‖
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi L
                        %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left\Vert \operatorname{X}f\right\Vert
                  _{L^q\big(\sigma\mapsto L^r_x(\mathbb{R}^{n-1})\big)}
                  \\;\le\;
                  C\left\Vert f\right\Vert_{L^p(\mathbb{R}^n)}.
          %p
            For brevity we will write
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi L
                      %mi σ
                      %mi q
                    %msubsup
                      %mi L
                      %mi x
                      %mi r
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ↦
                    %msubsup
                      %mi L
                      %mi x
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^q_\sigma L^r_x \coloneqq L^q\big(\sigma\mapsto L^r_x(\mathbb{R}^{n-1})\big)
          %p
            We can write the X-ray transform of a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi C
                    %mi c
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\in C_c^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
            as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∫
                  %mi f
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\operatorname{X} f(l)
                  \=
                  \\int f\delta_{l}(x)\,d
                  \\,,x
          %p
            where
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi l
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %mi ε
                        %mo →
                        %mn 0
                    %msup
                      %mi ε
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi l
                        %mo ∩
                        %msub
                          %mi B
                          %mi ε
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≠
                        %mi ∅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_{l} \coloneqq \lim_{\varepsilon\to 0}\varepsilon^{-n+1}1_{\{x\in\mathbb{R}^n\mid \;l\cap B_\varepsilon(x)\neq\emptyset\}}
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\sigma,x)
            is a line
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi l
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l\in M_n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_\sigma
            the projection to the plane
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{y\mid \langle y,\sigma\rangle = 0\}
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi l
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_l
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+a+distribution"} pullback
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi P
                      %mi σ
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_\sigma^*\delta_x = \delta_x\circ P_\sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_x
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+delta+distribution"} Dirac delta distribution
            centered at
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in\mathbb{R}^{n-1}
          %p
            The operator dual to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{X}
            %em i.e.
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                    %mi h
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi d
                    %mi μ
                    %mo =
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi h
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                      %mo *
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi dx
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int \operatorname{X}h\,f\,d\mu = \int h\,\operatorname{X}^*f\,dx
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_n
            as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                    %mo *
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∫
                  %mi f
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\operatorname{X}^*f(x) = \int f\delta_{\{x\}}(l)\,d\mu(l);
          %p
            here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mrow
                      %mi ε
                      %mo →
                      %mn 0
                  %msup
                    %mi ε
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi l
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi l
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi ε
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≠
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_{\{x\}} \coloneqq \lim_{\varepsilon\to 0}\varepsilon^{-n+1}1_{\{l\in M_n\mid \;l\cap B_\varepsilon(x)\neq\emptyset\}}
            — this is a distribution in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+delta+distribution"} Dirac delta distribution
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_x
            centered at
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_{\{x\}}
            is the restriction of the measure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_n
            to the set of lines passing through
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in\mathbb{R}^n
          %p The first bound we can get for the X-ray transform is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∫
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≤
                  %mo ∫
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∫
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                    %mo *
                  %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi dx
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∫
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi dx
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\int \vert \operatorname{X} f\vert\,d\mu(l) \le \int \operatorname{X}\vert f\vert\,1\,d\mu(l) = \int \vert f\vert\,\operatorname{X}^*1\,dx = \int \vert f\vert\,dx,
          %p
            since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                    %mo *
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{X}^*1
            is constant. Alternatively, we can use the fact that the integral of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{X}\vert f\vert
            along all the lines with the same direction equals
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo ‖
                        %mi f
                        %mo ‖
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left\Vert f\right\Vert_1
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{X}:L^1(\mathbb{R}^n)\to L^1(M_n)
          %p
            Besides
            = succeed "-spaces," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^p
          #SobolevSlobodeckij.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sobolev+space"}> Sobolev space
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform"} Fourier transform
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support+of+a+function"} supported
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo ∼
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert\xi\vert\sim 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{\varphi}
              be a smooth function with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform"} Fourier transform
              supported in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo ≲
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert\xi\vert\lesssim 1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mi k
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    1 = \sum_{k\ge 0}\varphi_k,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ≔
                    %mover
                      %mi φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi_0 \coloneqq \tilde{\varphi}
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi φ
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi_k(\xi) \coloneqq \varphi(\xi/2^k)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\ge 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_k
              be the projection
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mi k
                      %mi f
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∧
                      %mo ≔
                      %msub
                        %mi φ
                        %mi k
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (P_k f)^\wedge \coloneqq \varphi_k \hat{f}
            %p
              The Sobolev-Slobodeckij spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ,
                        %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W^{s,p}(\mathbb{R}^n)
              are, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi p
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\lt p\lt \infty
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi s
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\infty\lt s\lt \infty
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi W
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} [
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mi sk
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi k
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi L
                          %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi p
                    %msup
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ]
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                    %mtext if
                    %mphantom
                      %mo .
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∉
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Vert f\Vert_{W^{s,p}(\mathbb{R}^n)} := \Big[\sum_{k\ge 0}(2^{sk}\Vert P_k f\Vert_{L^p(\mathbb{R}^n)})^p\Big]^\frac{1}{p}\quad \text{if}\phantom{.} s \notin \mathbb{N},
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi W
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} [
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %msup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi α
                    %mi f
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi L
                          %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi p
                    %msup
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ]
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                    %mtext if
                    %mphantom
                      %mo .
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Vert f\Vert_{W^{s,p}(\mathbb{R}^n)} \coloneqq \Big[\sum_{\vert\alpha\vert\le s}\Vert \partial^\alpha f\Vert_{L^p(\mathbb{R}^n)}^p\Big]^\frac{1}{p} \quad \text{if}\phantom{.} s \in \mathbb{N}.
            %p
              See (
              %a{:href => "#triebel1978"}> Triebel 1978, Sec. 2.3.1
              ).
          %p The relation between that X-ray transform and the Kakeya set conjecture is the content of the following Theorem:
          #ThmXRayKakeya.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a{:href => "#bourgain1991"}> Bourgain 1991, Lemma 2.15
                )
            %p
              Let
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi s
                      %mi p
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n - s p\gt 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi supp
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi f
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} supp\,f\subset K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              compact, it holds that
            #eq:eqThmXRayKakeya.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi L
                          %mi σ
                          %mn 1
                        %msubsup
                          %mi L
                          %mi x
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi M
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi W
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Vert \operatorname{X} f\Vert_{L^1_\sigma L^\infty_x(M_n)}\le C_K\Vert f\Vert_{W^{s,p}(\mathbb{R}^n)},
            %p
              then the Hausdorff dimension of a Kakeya set is at least
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi s
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n- s p
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              To compute the Hausdorff dimension we can use either balls
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_r(x)
              or dyadic cubes
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mi k
                      %mo :
                      %mi l
                      %mo ≔
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi l
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mi k
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi l
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mi k
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_k :l\coloneqq [l2^k,(l+1)2^k]^n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              integer. In fact, we can cover a cube
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_k
              with a ball of radius
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msqrt
                        %mi n
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt{n}2^{k-1}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              with a few cubes
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_k
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi r
                      %mo ≤
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^{k-1}\lt r\le 2^k
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\subset\mathbb{R}^n
              be a Kakeya set. Give any covering
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} = \{Q_k\}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              at scale
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi δ
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\lt\delta\le 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_k\in\mathcal{C}
              its side-length is
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mi k
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^k\le\delta
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi d
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mi s
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\le d\lt n - s p
              then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Q
                          %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒞
                    %mi l
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi d
                    %mo →
                    %mn ∞
                    %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                    %mtext as
                    %mphantom
                      %mo .
                    %mi δ
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sum_{Q_k\in\mathcal{C}}l(Q_k)^d \to \infty \quad \text{as}\phantom{.}\delta\to 0,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi l
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l(Q_k) = 2^k
              is the side-length of the cube.
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a covering of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              at scale
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_k
              the collection of all the cubes in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              with side-length
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_k
              the union of all the cubes in
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_k
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi E
                    %mo ≤
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi k
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Q
                          %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Q
                          %mi k
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    1_E \le \sum_k 1_{A_k} \coloneqq \sum_k \Big(\sum_{Q_k\in\mathcal{C}_k}1_{Q_k}\Big).
            %p
              Since our hypotheses involve the spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi W
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo ,
                          %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W^{s,p}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_{A_k}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
              with compact support, define the dilations
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi φ
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi l
                      %mo ≔
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi nk
                      %mi φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi_k(x) \colon l\coloneqq 2^{-nk}\varphi(x/2^k)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_{A_k}
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi φ
                        %mi k
                      %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi_k*1_{A_k}
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              contains a unit line segment in every direction
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℙ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma\in \mathbb{P}^{n-1}
              it holds that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mo ,
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi L
                            %mn ∞
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Vert \operatorname{X}1_E(\cdot,\sigma)\Vert_{L^\infty} \ge 1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi L
                          %mi σ
                          %mn 1
                        %msubsup
                          %mi L
                          %mi x
                          %mn ∞
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi C
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mn 2
                          %mi k
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mi k
                    %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi k
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi L
                          %mi σ
                          %mn 1
                        %msubsup
                          %mi L
                          %mi x
                          %mn ∞
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    1\le \Vert \operatorname{X}1_E\Vert_{L^1_\sigma L^\infty_x}\le C\sum_{2^k\le\delta}\Vert \operatorname{X}\big(\varphi_k*1_{A_k}\big)\Vert_{L^1_\sigma L^\infty_x}.
            %p
              By
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:eqThmXRayKakeya"} (1)
              we have that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≤
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi C
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mn 2
                          %mi k
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mi k
                    %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi W
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %mi p
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    1
                    \\;\le\; C\sum_{2^k\le\delta} \Vert \varphi_k*1_{A_k}\Vert_{W^{s,p}}.
            %p
              In general, the
              = succeed "-norm" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi W
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo ,
                          %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W^{s,p}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mi k
                    %mo *
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi_k*f
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mi k
                    %mo *
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi W
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %mi p
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi C
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi ks
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi p
                    %mo ;
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Vert \varphi_k*f\Vert_{W^{s,p}}\le C2^{-ks}\Vert f\Vert_p;
            %p
              see Lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LemmSobolevConv"}
              below. Hence,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi C
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mn 2
                          %mi k
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mi k
                    %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi W
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %mi p
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi C
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mn 2
                          %mi k
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi δ
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi ks
                        %mo +
                        %mfrac
                          %mi nk
                          %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    1\le C\sum_{2^k\le\delta} \Vert \varphi_k*1_{A_k}\Vert_{W^{s,p}} \le C\sum_{2^k\le\delta}2^{-ks+\frac{nk}{p}}\vert \mathcal{C}_k\vert^\frac{1}{p}
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert \mathcal{C}_k\vert
              denotes the number of cubes in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_k
            %p
              By hypothesis
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi s
                      %mi p
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-s p\gt 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi d
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mi sp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\le d \lt n-sp
              we can apply Hölder inequality to get
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mn 2
                          %mi k
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi δ
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ′
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mi d
                          %mi p
                        %mo −
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo ′
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mi kd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msup
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi p
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi C
                    %msup
                      %mi δ
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Q
                          %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒞
                    %mi l
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi p
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    1 \le \Big(\sum_{2^k\le\delta} 2^{p'k(\frac{n-d}{p}-s)}\Big)^\frac{1}{p'}\Big(\sum_k 2^{kd}\vert\mathcal{C}_k\vert\Big)^\frac{1}{p} \le C\delta^\alpha\Big(\sum_{Q_k\in\mathcal{C}}l(Q_k)^d\Big)^\frac{1}{p},
            %p
              where
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo =
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mi d
                        %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mi s
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha = \frac{n-d}{p}-s\gt 0
          #LemmSobolevConv.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
              is a smooth function and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ψ
                        %mi l
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi l
                      %mo ≔
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mi nl
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mi l
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi_l(x) :l\coloneqq 2^{nl}\psi(2^l x)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi l
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l\ge 0
            #eq:LemmSobolevConv.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi l
                    %mo *
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi W
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi C
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mi ls
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi p
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Vert \psi_l*f\Vert_{W^{s,p}(\mathbb{R}^n)}\le C2^{ls}\Vert f\Vert_p,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              depends on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ψ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LemmSobolevConv"} (2)
              follows from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi l
                    %mo *
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi l
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial^\alpha(\psi_l*f) = (\partial^\alpha \psi_l)*f
              and from the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Young+inequality+for+convolutions"} Young inequality for convolutions
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ≠
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\neq
              integer, then we have to estimate the norm of
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mi k
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_k f
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mi k
                      %mi f
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∧
                      %mo ≔
                      %msub
                        %mi φ
                        %mi k
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (P_k f)^\wedge \coloneqq \varphi_k \hat{f}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi φ
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi_k(\xi) \coloneqq \varphi(\xi/2^k)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi l
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\le l
              then by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Young+inequality+for+convolutions"} Young inequality for convolutions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi l
                    %mo *
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi p
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi φ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˇ
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi l
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi p
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi p
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Vert P_k(\psi_l*f)\Vert_p \le \Vert \check{\varphi}_k\Vert_1\Vert \psi_l\Vert_1\Vert f\Vert_p \le C\Vert f\Vert_p.
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mi l
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\gt l
              then fix a number
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi N
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2N\gt s
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi k
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_k f
              as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi l
                    %mo *
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi p
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi ξ
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 2
                        %mi N
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∨
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi l
                    %mo *
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi p
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Vert P_k(\psi_l*f)\Vert_p \le \Vert (\vert \xi\vert^{-2N}\varphi_k)^\vee\Vert_1 \Vert \Delta^N(\psi_l*f)\Vert_p.
            %p
              As before we get
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ψ
                        %mi l
                      %mo *
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi p
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi C
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mi N
                          %mi l
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi f
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Vert \Delta^N (\psi_l*f)\Vert_p\le C 2^{2 N l}\Vert f\Vert_p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi ξ
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 2
                        %mi N
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∨
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 2
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi ξ
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 2
                        %mi N
                    %mi φ
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∨
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mi k
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\vert \xi\vert^{-2N}\varphi_k)^\vee(x) = 2^{(n-2 N)k}(\vert \xi\vert^{-2N}\varphi)^\vee(2^k x)
              then we get
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi ξ
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 2
                        %mi N
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∨
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msup
